# Parity and codegen

`tools/runtime-taxonomy/manifest.mjs` is the **only** authority for public runtime subpaths. Codegen propagates manifest entries into each package — hand-editing without updating the source chain creates drift.

## Manifest entry shape

Each `RuntimeAtomEntry` must define:

| Field | Required | Notes |
|-------|----------|-------|
| `type` | Yes | Dotted taxonomy key; permanent once shipped |
| `subpath` | Yes | kebab path after `@rosettadash/<runtime>/` |
| `exportName` | Yes | PascalCase symbol |
| `pattern` | Yes | `native` \| `manual` \| `ce-host` |
| `kind` | If `native` | Template id in `*-templates.mjs` |
| `testId` | Yes | Equals BEM root / `data-testid` |
| `wcImport` | If CE-host | WC subpath for framework wrappers |

Add NPM recipes via `NPM_RECIPE_ENTRIES`, not ad-hoc exports.

## Codegen commands

| Command | Package |
|---------|---------|
| `npm run generate:web-components-runtime` | web-components |
| `npm run generate:react-runtime` | react |
| `npm run generate:angular-runtime` | angular |
| `npm run generate:vue-runtime` | vue |
| `npm run generate:svelte-runtime` | svelte |

Flags: `--write` applies changes; `--force` overwrites existing generated files.

## Generated vs hand-written

| Generated (skip if exists unless `--force`) | Never generated — hand-maintained |
|---------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| Native atom component + spec + index | `pattern: 'manual'` WC CEs and CE-hosts |
| Barrel indexes, root exports maps | NPM recipe atoms (accordion, link-list) |
| WC native atoms from `wc-templates.mjs` | Catalog CEs, browser/media bundle |
| | Full Three.js beyond template stub |
| | React-only extras (see charter grandfather list) |
| | `custom-element-host` libs per framework |

**Rule:** If you edit a generated file, either (a) promote the change into `tools/runtime-taxonomy/*-templates.mjs` and re-run codegen with `--force`, or (b) change manifest `pattern` to `manual` with a parity ticket.

## Pattern selection

| Pattern | Choose when |
|---------|-------------|
| `native` | DOM is static or templated; no shadow DOM; shared markup in templates |
| `manual` | Shadow DOM media, map providers, wasm CE, complex lifecycle |
| `ce-host` | WC exists; framework is a thin wrapper (`wcImport` set) |

## Skip-existing behavior

Codegen logs `skip existing <subpath>` when a file already exists. This preserves hand-enhancements (e.g. React `BarChart` with axis labels). Before merging enhancements:

1. Decide if enhancement belongs in shared template (all runtimes) or is grandfathered single-runtime debt.
2. If shared → update `react-templates.mjs` (kind props/bodies) and `--force` all runtimes.

## Legitimate divergence (rare)

Allowed only with:

1. DAS parity ticket naming the gap and target close date
2. Entry in charter **Grandfathered debt** (temporary — do not extend list)
3. Storybook/catalog note visible to consumers

**Never** ship a new framework-only export without manifest + ticket.

## Parity verification (manual until automated)

Before calling a component done across runtimes:

- [ ] Subpath in all five `package.json` exports maps
- [ ] Same `exportName` and props surface
- [ ] Same root `rd-*` + `data-testid`
- [ ] Storybook catalog row in all five apps (shared `tools/storybook-shared/`)
- [ ] Jest spec in each runtime package

## Shared templates

- `react-templates.mjs` — `KIND_PROPS`, `KIND_BODIES` (shared kind markup reference)
- `wc-templates.mjs`, `angular-templates.mjs`, `vue-templates.mjs`, `svelte-templates.mjs` — per-target renderers
- `taxonomyTypeToBemBlock()` in manifest — use for `testId`, never invent alternate BEM roots

